{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bleareyed-claimable-quelea","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"Spun from 73d8 (brainy-convulsant-unicorn) and 551b (sanidine-cilium-eland) during the 2026-08-30 error-code decision pass.\n\n## Problem\n`error_code_for` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`) branch 6 maps ANY `LLMError → llm_unavailable`. That over-claims an AI-provider outage for many faults that are not outages — every non-availability `LLMError`/`WorkflowError` subclass (editor missing-bundle, workflow parse/wiring, etc.). This is the residual of origin 8a31's blanket mapping and the systematic completion of epic 3405's descriptiveness intent.\n\n## Fix\nNarrow branch 6 so `llm_unavailable` fires ONLY for `LLMUnavailableError` (the true transient-outage type). Every other `LLMError` subclass falls through to its explicit `error_code` attribute (branch 5) if it has one, else to `command_failed` (branch 7) — honest \"unclassified\", not a false outage.\n\n## Blast radius (must sweep)\nEnumerate ALL `LLMError` subclasses (`src/rebar/llm/errors.py` + workflow error classes). For each, confirm the post-change code is correct: a genuine transient outage must remain `LLMUnavailableError → llm_unavailable`; anything else must land on an accurate code. Add held-out tests through real surfaces proving (a) an execute-time outage still returns `llm_unavailable`, (b) a non-outage `WorkflowError` (e.g. the editor missing-bundle at `editor.py:475`) returns `command_failed`.\n\n## Resolves 551b\nThis delivers 551b's ruling: editor missing-bundle → `command_failed`, no new vocabulary. The finer `environment_unready` code for a missing local build artifact stays DEFERRED (revisit trigger: `edit_workflow` becoming classifier-reachable on a live MCP surface); analysis retained on 551b.\n\n## Coordination\nTouches `src/rebar/llm/` = eb64 (financial-stoneware-brant) DECLARED SCOPE. Implement in coordination with eb64. `_errors.py` itself is top-level (not eb64).\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] branch 6 narrowed to `LLMUnavailableError`; all other `LLMError` subclasses sweep-verified to accurate codes.\n- [ ] Held-out tests: outage → `llm_unavailable`; editor missing-bundle → `command_failed`; through real surfaces.\n- [ ] caused_by 8a31 recorded at close.","id":"ce6b-cffa-6450-4fa5","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["error-codes","llm","eb64-coord"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reserve llm_unavailable for true outages: narrow error_code_for branch 6 to LLMUnavailableError"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788109253593886326,"uuid":"7e3736f3-4506-49cc-86b8-caa6b4f60319"}